A||N||12||Fatal Error||3.1 turbo & intercooler||||5||
Z||000000||Fatal Error||08-02-2001||07:13 PM||||How much HP should one get from this setup?<BR>Thanks guys!<P>-Fatal||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rogue_Ant||08-02-2001||07:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fatal Error:<BR><B>How much HP should one get from this setup?<BR>Thanks guys!<P>-Fatal</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Lol thats a broad question, it depends.  On how much boost you run, how well your engine breathes, cam profile, intake temp., ignition quality, ect.<BR>But if you do a decent job I don't think 50% hp increase is unreasonable.  So say ~140 for the 3.1L, add 70hp for the turbo and intercooler = ~210hp.<P>Rogue<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fatal Error||08-02-2001||08:03 PM||||LOl .. hahaha your right, I guess I didn't think about that. Ok here goes. I thought that doing the 2.8 to 3.1 upgrade was supposed to give you a good solid 30 hp (from 135 to 165) increase because of displacement??? Anyhow a 3.1 with the best of everything.. high perf cam .. built heads / ported & polished .. headers .. no cat .. MSD stuff .. <P>What are the benefits of a twin turbo over a single turbo? What is the max boost a 3.1 could handle (without having to rebuild ever week)? Also, how much can it take if you start throwing nitrous into the picture?<P>Is it possible to get a good 300hp out of a 3.1 setup? <P>Thanks!<P>-Fatal  ||||reg||10
Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||08-02-2001||10:39 PM||||Keep the comp. low when you build that 3.1<BR>or you'll be sorry. It would be a good idea to keep the comp. at 8.5:1 or lower. Check this web-site out for some ideas. <A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nbci.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm</A> <P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||4
Z||000004||Rogue_Ant||08-02-2001||11:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fatal Error:<BR><B><BR>What are the benefits of a twin turbo over a single turbo? What is the max boost a 3.1 could handle (without having to rebuild ever week)? Also, how much can it take if you start throwing nitrous into the picture?<P>Is it possible to get a good 300hp out of a 3.1 setup? <P>Thanks!<BR>-Fatal  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>How much boost depends on a few things, your compression rating, your intake temperature, and timming (and a couple of other things).  If you go with a low compression (i.e. 7.5to1) you can have quite a bit of boost.  Also the better your intercooler the more boost your engine can handle.  You will need to use a Boost Timming Retard though to retard your timming as boost increases - this is pretty easy to do with MSD stuff though.<BR>The reason you would use twin turbos is so that you can use two smaller turbos to produce the same amount of boost one larger one would - but since they are smaller they spool up quicker and have less 'lag' time.<BR>I don't see why a performance built tubro 3.1 couldn't make 300hp, although using a 3.4 block to start with would be easier (and maybe more practical) since it is a little bigger, and have newer heads.<P>Rogue||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fatal Error||08-03-2001||12:13 AM||||Rogue Ant Thanks for the info! As far as the 3.4 .. why wouldnt one just step on up to the 4.3 v6? it's just the same as a sbc 350 ... just shy 2 cyl. .. I've heard of 4.3's super crazy setup to pump out over 600hp .. not that i would ever need anything near that ...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Thanks!<P>-Fatal||||reg||10
Z||000006||Rogue_Ant||08-03-2001||01:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fatal Error:<BR><B>Rogue Ant Thanks for the info! As far as the 3.4 .. why wouldnt one just step on up to the 4.3 v6? it's just the same as a sbc 350 ... just shy 2 cyl. .. I've heard of 4.3's super crazy setup to pump out over 600hp .. not that i would ever need anything near that ...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Thanks!<P>-Fatal</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well I say a 3.4 because it is the same block as the 2.8(3.1 ect).  It is almost a direct bolt in since it is still a 60degree V-6.  You can make a 3.4 look almost identical to a normal 2.8!<BR>The 4.3 is a very good engine and it is true it is basically a SBC shy 2 cyl.  But this is a much tougher swap.  Now you have to get a kit to adapt it to your tranny, all kinds of wiring and computer modifications, fabricate water pump and other accessories, yadda yadda, ect.<P>Rogue<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Will||08-03-2001||02:11 AM||||Grand Prix Turbo 3.1's made 225HP stock, and should be a fairly easy swap. 300 HP shouldn't be too much trouble.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fatal Error||08-03-2001||03:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rogue_Ant:<BR><B> Well I say a 3.4 because it is the same block as the 2.8(3.1 ect).  It is almost a direct bolt in since it is still a 60degree V-6.  You can make a 3.4 look almost identical to a normal 2.8!<BR>The 4.3 is a very good engine and it is true it is basically a SBC shy 2 cyl.  But this is a much tougher swap.  Now you have to get a kit to adapt it to your tranny, all kinds of wiring and computer modifications, fabricate water pump and other accessories, yadda yadda, ect.<P>Rogue<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>How hard is it to do a swap from an I4 setup to a 3.4? I'm sure I could find one at junkyard. I'm very new to all of this .. so please forgive me if I seem a bit intimidated. Thanks for all the help and the info!.<P>-Fatal||||reg||6
Z||000009||Rogue_Ant||08-04-2001||10:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fatal Error:<BR><B> <BR>How hard is it to do a swap from an I4 setup to a 3.4? I'm sure I could find one at junkyard. I'm very new to all of this .. so please forgive me if I seem a bit intimidated. Thanks for all the help and the info!.<P>-Fatal</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Well the 3.4 should bolt right up to your tranny, so thats good.  But it would be easier if you had a 2.8 or access to one, since you will need all the accessories off of it, computer, wiring harness, and pretty much the top half of the engine.  But it is still much easier then a 4.3 or SBC swap.<BR>Oh remember on a 3.4 you will need to get a shop to put the starter on the otherside of the engine.<P>Rogue<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||terryk||08-05-2001||01:49 AM||||I think the GP-T was rated 205HP.||||reg||1
Z||000011||rogergarrison||08-05-2001||10:06 AM||||I have a built up 3.1 with one turbo. its 8.5 compression. I thought about adding a intercooler from MR2 (opps). But when it was finished it dynoed to around 275 hp. I normally run between 4-5 pnds boost and have tried up to 12. Im sure its prob lost some since Ive put over 85k on engine now. I have turbo dialed in to come on to power around 2500 rpm so I have no lag whatsoever. Ive got my redline at a bit above 7000 rpm where the rev limiters set. I drive it daily and its been very reliable and plenty fast enough for me.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Smoooooth GT||08-05-2001||10:45 AM||||Roger....  Sound's like FUN....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <BR>BUT... I just bought Shaun's... NOS Kit so...  lol  Here I come too...  Steve<P>------------------<BR>NEW EMAIL..  Smooth_gt@k.st<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_3.JPG">     <BR>  with a 100-125HP shot of NOS...||||reg||1
